1. Overview
-----------

FriESP is an embedded systems project that turns an ESP32 microcontroller into
a small electronic character with animated facial expressions. The character
is designed to react to its environment: temperature changes alter its
expression (feeling hot or cold), and movement or rotation makes it look
dizzy.

The project combines three areas of embedded development:

- Graphics rendering on a small TFT display.
- Sensor integration (temperature and motion).
- Interactive behavior driven by buttons and environmental data.

Development is incremental and validated on physical hardware at every stage.

